  "$aircraftComment": "Curated, because MSFS 2024 packages are opaque .fsarchive blobs and the four facts cannot be read from disk (verified 2026-09-03). 'match' is the substring FSUIPC matches the sim's aircraft title on, and doubles as the profile name. 'facts' are what the classification rule needs; 'layout' is what they resolve to. 'verified' says how the entry is known: flown means the levers were seen driving the right controls in the sim; type means it follows from the aircraft type and has not been flown yet. Add an aircraft only with both facts answered - never guess them.",
  "aircraft": [
